senses.gloss:
करम्बित, अस्, आ, अम्, intermingled, mixed,
blended, &c.; pounded, reduced to grains or dust;
set, inlaid.

करुत्थाम करुत्थाम, अस्, m., N. of a
prince, a son of Dushyanta and father of Ākrīḍa;
[cf. अश्वत्थामन्.]

कार्दम कार्दम, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कर्दम),
made of mud, muddy, filled or covered with it;
belonging to Prajāpati Kardama.

कर्बूर or कर्वूर, अस्, m. a Rakṣas; the plant
Curcuma Amhaldi or Zerumbet; (आ), f. a leech;
(अम्), n. gold; a yellow orpiment.

कर्मिन्, ई, इणी, इ, acting, active, busy; performing
a religious action; engaged in any work or business;
belonging or relating to any act.

कर्वर 2. कर्वर or कर्बर, अस्, आ, अम् (said
to be fr. rt. 1. कॄ), variegated, spotted; (अस्), m. sin;
a tiger; a Rakṣas; a sort of medicament; (ई), f.
an epithet of Durgā; night; a Rākṣasī; a tigress;
the leaf of the plant Asa Fœtida; [cf. करवी, कवरी,
कारवी.] See कर्बुर.

कार्श्य 1. कार्श्य, अस्, m., N. of several
plants, = कार्ष्य and कार्ष्मर्य, = कर्चूर;
another plant, Artocarpus Lacucha.

कारेणव कारेणव, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. करेणु),
produced by or coming from the female elephant;
a patronymic of Pālakāpya.

कार्त्स्न कार्त्स्न, अम्, n. (fr. कृत्स्न), the
whole, totality, all, entireness; (perhaps a wrong form
for the following.)

1. कार्मुक, अस्, ई, अम्, finishing a work, doing
it well or completely, fit for or able to do a work;
(अस्), m. a bamboo.

कार्षि, इस्, इस्, इ, Ved. drawing, attracting; plough-
ing; (इस्), m. fire; (इस्), f. drawing, attracting;
ploughing, cultivation.
